      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Amazon</span><span class=\"chip company\">Google</span><span class=\"chip company\">Stripe</span><span class=\"chip company\">Atlassian</span><span class=\"chip company\">Uber</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Distributed Rate Limiter</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">You already know token buckets from QoS policers. This page shows how the same idea works when 50 API gateways must share one limit per user: the four classic algorithms (with a runnable comparison), Redis plus Lua for atomic checks, what to do when Redis dies, and the follow-ups interviewers always ask.</p>\n      "
